-- lib/ceptr.cub — Hyperactive Receptivity (docs/hyperactive-receptivity.md, §6 "Protocols"): Ceptr's protocols
-- (github.com/zippy/ceptr, src/base_defs and src/protocol.c) as choreographies over roles, from which each
-- role's behaviour is the endpoint projection (lib/proc.cub: Chor, project, Projectable). A protocol is a
-- function of its semantic references: its ROLEs are role words and its USAGEs are the symbols carried, so a
-- RESOLUTION is application and a LINKAGE is a renaming; an INCLUSION is the included protocol with its
-- references renamed and resolved (Ceptr's _o_unwrap); expressing a role (Ceptr's _o_express_role) is the
-- projection, defined on projectable protocols. Ceptr's own base protocols are instances: REQUESTING,
-- RECOGNIZE (REQUESTING included with linkages and resolutions), ALIVE, and the group protocol's two
-- interactions. Each is projectable by computation, and RECOGNIZE as an inclusion of REQUESTING equals
-- REQUESTING applied to its resolved references, by computation.
import "core.cub"
import "proc.cub"
